usage: cybersec [-h]
                {init,scanner-worker,evidence,target,job,finding,artifact,report,alert,api,remote} ...

Authorized security assessment orchestrator with evidence auditing and bounded
scanner workers.

positional arguments:
  {init,scanner-worker,evidence,target,job,finding,artifact,report,alert,api,remote}
    init                Initialize local database
    scanner-worker      Run a dedicated durable scanner-job worker
    evidence            Verify portable evidence artifacts offline without
                        database access
    target              Manage authorized assessment targets
    job                 Manage scan jobs
    finding             Manage normalized findings
    artifact            Import, search, inspect, and replay stored scanner
                        artifacts
    report              Export project data
    alert               Manage local alert policies, queue, and opt-in webhook
                        delivery
    api                 Serve the token-protected loopback HTTP API; does not
                        run scanners
    remote              Use the token-protected loopback API client; metadata
                        operations only

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
